# NVIDIA's CUDA repository for Debian 13, flat (sources.list(5): "suite can specify an exact path, in which case the
# components must be omitted and suite must end with a slash"), read for amd64 and i386: NVIDIA's i386 driver libraries
# (OpenGL, Vulkan, CUDA) are what Steam's, Wine's and 32-bit games need on an NVIDIA card, and a Multi-Arch: same library
# must be at the same version on both architectures (Debian Policy 5.6.34.3), so they come from here, at the version of the
# amd64 driver; dpkg installs them only where it has i386. CUDA itself is 64-bit. Signed-By names NVIDIA's own key file,
# the one NVIDIA's cuda-keyring installs, so a source written NVIDIA's way names the same key (apt refuses two sources for
# one URI with different Signed-By).
# sparky-stereo-cuda-repo's postinst writes this file, from /usr/share/sparky-stereo-cuda-repo, when no other source of apt
# names this repository, and its postrm removes it; 91sparky-stereo-cuda holds the pins.
Types: deb
URIs: https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/repos/debian13/x86_64/
Suites: /
Architectures: amd64 i386
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/cuda-archive-keyring.gpg
